  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Mark the right way – five v five",
  "description": "Two teams of four outfield players and a keeper each. Use the whole rink, or shorten it with cones if five a side feels too thin. The teams take turns to attack: one team gets five attacks in a row, then you swap. Each attack starts with a throw from the team's own keeper. Offside applies.\n\nThe defending team marks and tries to win the ball. An attempt ends when the defence wins the ball, a goal is scored or the ball goes over the boards or the end line. Count goals and won balls.\n\nVariation: play on after a won ball so that both teams can counter several times in the same attempt – it only ends with a goal or when the ball goes out. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Stay goal-side of your player, where you can see both the player and the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Close to the ball, mark tight; further away, drop off and help in the middle."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Skate with runs in behind – be ready to step in with your stick and cut out the pass."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Talk: say who you are taking and when you hand a player over."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
